 "turns": [
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hi! How's life treating you?",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.54,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_14"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I'm great, thanks.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.65,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_08"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "How often should I water my houseplants?",
   "est_sec": 2.27,
   "gap_before": 0.54,
   "block": "gardening.dlg1",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Most like to dry out a bit between waterings. Push a finger into the soil, and if the top few centimeters are dry, it's time.",
   "est_sec": 7.85,
   "gap_before": 0.4,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "gardening.dlg1"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Hold on, really?",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.74,
   "block": "gardening.dlg1",
   "kind": "wait_like",
   "phrasing": "waitlike_11",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hmm, I believe it is. Which part doesn't sound right?",
   "est_sec": 3.2,
   "gap_before": 1.19,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "gardening.dlg1"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "So not on a fixed schedule?",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 1.09,
   "block": "gardening.dlg1",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Not really. In winter they need much less, and in summer they might need it twice a week.",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 0.47,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "gardening.dlg1"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I have a cactus and a",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 0.92,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "gardening.dlg1"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "what's it called, a peace lily.",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 2.2,
   "block": "gardening.dlg1",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Those are opposites. Water the cactus maybe once a month, and the peace lily when its leaves start to droop a little.",
   "est_sec": 6.92,
   "gap_before": 0.47,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "gardening.dlg1"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Oh, it droops? I thought that meant it was dying.",
   "est_sec": 3.2,
   "gap_before": 0.66,
   "block": "gardening.dlg1",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "It's just being dramatic. Give it a good drink and it usually perks up within a few hours.",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 0.83,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "gardening.dlg1"
  }
 ]
}
